# v0.5 baseline recovery

The current checkout has uncommitted showcase/runtime changes, including files that differ from the v0.4 release baseline. Git correctly refused a checkout because doing so would overwrite those local changes.

Required safe recovery, with explicit user approval:

1. Preserve the current dirty checkout by copying or committing the showcase work in a separate user-owned change set.
2. Create/switch to a branch at tag `v0.4` (`bfb5f5b...`).
3. Reapply only the intended v0.5 planning files and v0.5 implementation files.
4. Do not carry demo showcase files into the v0.5 branch unless they are independently required by the v0.5 feature.

No destructive command was run; the attempted checkout was rejected by Git before changing files.
